BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Eskenazi Museum of Art
DTSTART:20261028T170000Z
DTEND:20261028T200000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Open Studio
DESCRIPTION:Our Open Studio program invites participants to create in the
  museum's art studio\, where art becomes a tool for reflection\, expressi
 on\, and connection. Guided by a trained art therapist\, the open studio 
 welcomes visitors to engage with materials at their own pace while drawin
 g inspiration from the surrounding exhibitions. No art experience is need
 ed\; just bring your curiosity and a desire to create\, and we'll handle 
 the rest!  This specific Open Studio is themed around the crown of IU's f
 ootball season: Homecoming Weekend! We will be providing t-shirts and sup
 plies for you to create your very own Game Day t-shirt!  This group meets
  on the 2nd and 4th Wednesday of every month\, excluding holidays and mus
 eum closures. It is open to everyone: students\, staff\, and the public i
 ncluded! The group will meet in the Roehm Family Art-making Studio\, loca
 ted inside the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the Esken
 azi Museum of Art.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Our Open Studio program invites partici
 pants to create in the museum's art studio\, where art becomes a tool for
  reflection\, expression\, and connection. Guided by a trained art therap
 ist\, the open studio welcomes visitors to engage with materials at their
  own pace while drawing inspiration from the surrounding exhibitions. No 
 art experience is needed\; just bring your curiosity and a desire to crea
 te\, and we'll handle the rest!</p><p>  This specific Open Studio is them
 ed around the crown of IU's football season: Homecoming Weekend! We will 
 be providing t-shirts and supplies for you to create your very own Game D
 ay t-shirt!</p><p>  This group meets on the 2nd and 4th Wednesday of ever
 y month\, excluding holidays and museum closures. It is open to everyone:
  students\, staff\, and the public included! The group will meet in the R
 oehm Family Art-making Studio\, located inside the Simpson Center for Edu
 cation on the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi Museum of Art.</p>
