DTSTART:20261105T210000Z
DTEND:20261105T223000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Art That Changed Me: One Image\, One Story
DESCRIPTION:Art can be anything that inspires us—a painting\, a buildin
 g\, a fashion collection\, a photograph\, a piece of music\, a place\, or
  even an everyday object that changes the way we see the world.  In colla
 boration with the Art Therapy Program at the Eskenazi Museum\, Art That C
 hanged Me invites attendees to share one image (physical or digital) and 
 one story about something that has inspired\, challenged\, or shaped who 
 they are.  Through brief 3–5 minute presentations\, participants will c
 elebrate the diverse experiences\, passions\, and creative journeys that 
 make up our community while exploring the powerful connections between cr
 eativity\, reflection\, and wellbeing.  Participants are encouraged to br
 ing their content ready to go on a flash drive to enable ease of loading 
 in for their presentations quickly.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Art can be anything that inspires us—
 a painting\, a building\, a fashion collection\, a photograph\, a piece o
 f music\, a place\, or even an everyday object that changes the way we se
 e the world.</p><p>  In collaboration with the Art Therapy Program at the
  Eskenazi Museum\, <i>Art That Changed Me</i> invites attendees to share 
 one image (physical or digital) and one story about something that has in
 spired\, challenged\, or shaped who they are.</p><p>  Through brief 3–5
  minute presentations\, participants will celebrate the diverse experienc
 es\, passions\, and creative journeys that make up our community while ex
 ploring the powerful connections between creativity\, reflection\, and we
 llbeing.</p><p class="elementToProof">  Participants are encouraged to br
 ing their content ready to go on a flash drive to enable ease of loading 
 in for their presentations quickly.</p>
