LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Art as a Representation of Sustainability: Preserving Culture\, E
 nvironment\, and Economic Vitality
DESCRIPTION:Highlighting a variety of works in the Eskenazi Museum of Art
 \, including the Samuel Levi Jones: An Archeology of Knowledge exhibition
 \, we'll consider sustainability beyond the environment and explore what 
 we value—and hope for —in building a future for generations to come.A
 bout Your Guide  Blake Nietert is a Marketing\, International\, and Susta
 inable Business major with a minor in Art History. With five semesters of
  experience leading tours at the Eskenazi Museum of Art\, he is slowly co
 nvincing himself that he has seen the artworks move when no one is watchi
 ng.  While especially passionate about European art\, Blake loves explori
 ng and researching art from around the world. He finds that the Eskenazi 
 Museum of Art always offers a new perspective on life when he needs it mo
 st. Blake leads Art Investigator Tours\, Teen Gallery Walks\, and a varie
 ty of specialty tours\, sharing his enthusiasm for art and creating engag
 ing experiences for museum visitors  &#160\;  Know Before You GoWalk-ins 
 are welcome if space is available. Check in with Guest Services on the fi
 rst floor.&#160\;A small handbag may be carried at your side. Backpacks a
 nd large bags will need to be stored before touring. Learn more aboutmuse
 um guidelines.If you park in the IMU parking lot\, Guest Services can val
 idate your parking voucher for a discount.Read aboutwhere to find us and 
 where to park\,
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Highlighting a variety of works in the 
 Eskenazi Museum of Art\, including the <i>Samuel Levi Jones: An Archeolog
 y of Knowledge</i> exhibition\, we'll consider sustainability beyond the 
 environment and explore what we value—and hope for —in building a fut
 ure for generations to come.<br /><br /><strong>About Your Guide</strong>
 </p><p data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">  Blake Nietert is a Marketing\
 , International\, and Sustainable Business major with a minor in Art Hist
 ory. With five semesters of experience leading tours at the Eskenazi Muse
 um of Art\, he is slowly convincing himself that he has seen the artworks
  move when no one is watching.</p><p>  While especially passionate about 
 European art\, Blake loves exploring and researching art from around the 
 world. He finds that the Eskenazi Museum of Art always offers a new persp
 ective on life when he needs it most. Blake leads Art Investigator Tours\
 , Teen Gallery Walks\, and a variety of specialty tours\, sharing his ent
 husiasm for art and creating engaging experiences for museum visitors</p>
