 .m.</strong> Lunch\, Martin Commons\, second floor</p><p style="font-weig
 ht: 400\;"><strong>1–2 p.m.</strong> Artist talk\, Learn more about Sus
 an's artistic journey\, creative philosophy\, and evolving practice\, fol
 lowed by an open Q+A session\, Martin Commons\, second floor</p><p style=
 "font-weight: 400\;"><strong>2–4 p.m.</strong> Enjoy hands-on artist pr
 ogramming and a rare look at selected objects from the museum's collectio
 ns.</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Susan Charlesworth is an award-win
 ning basket weaver who first began weaving in 2005\, when she entered her
  baskets into the Choctaw Nation Annual Labor Day Festival and Art Show. 
 Susan has continued to receive awards at multiple Native art markets\, in
 cluding the Eiteljorg Indian Market &amp\; Festival. Susan is a retired C
 NA and social service consultant with a master's degree in social work an
 d an avid volunteer with the Alzheimer's Association. She now serves as a
 n Alzheimer's Association Community Educator in Indianapolis.</p><div><p>
 <span class="TextRun SCXW242918722 BCX4" lang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" da
